window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: Eavesdropping","paragraphs":["\"Nah, Noah wouldn’t do that.\" Leonard spoke up for him. \"No matter how playful he can be, flirting with a woman old enough to be his mother isn’t something he’d do.\"","Noah immediately nodded. \"Exactly! How could I ever do something like that?\"","Lyria also nodded in agreement. \"I think so too. No matter how much of a tease Noah may be, I don’t think he would ever do something like that to an older woman.\"","Noah felt a little relieved hearing Lyria defend him. ’At least Lyria believes in me.’","Arisha, however, remained unconvinced.","She narrowed her yellow eyes at him for another moment before eventually returning her attention to her food.","\"Well, whatever. I still think you did something, but I’ll let it go.\"","She shrugged indifferently. \"It’s not my problem, anyway.\"","Noah felt a strange bitterness at her words. ’Why does it feel like she’s already decided I’m guilty?’","Still, there was no point in continuing the conversation. He quickly decided to change the subject.","\"So, what’s going to be different during our second semester?\"","\"No idea,\" Damien replied. \"Classes begin tomorrow, so I guess we’ll find out.\"","Draven immediately let out a heavy sigh. \"Ugh... boring classes. Lectures...\"","He looked thoroughly displeased.","Draven clearly preferred practical lessons where he could train, fight, and actually use his strength rather than sit through hours of lectures.","\"I understand you, brother.\"","Ragnar nodded seriously. The two of them clearly shared the same hatred for studying.","The group continued chatting while finishing their lunch, enjoying their first reunion after Noah’s long absence.","---","Later, Noah parted ways with his friends.","He had no particular plans for the rest of the afternoon, so he decided to return to his dormitory and rest for a while.","He had barely walked halfway there when he noticed someone familiar in the distance.","A young man with black hair was walking ahead of him.","Ken Takeane was also from the Raigamine Duchy, the Eastern Duchy where Akari came from.","He and Noah were classmates, and they had fought alongside each other during several practical exercises before.","Since they already knew each other, Noah decided to greet him. But before Noah could call out to him, Ken suddenly turned onto another path.","Noah stopped.","’...Huh?’","Ken was heading toward the back of the dormitory building.","That was the same area where Noah had previously made a deal with Travis and the others before their VR match.","’Why is he going there?’","Noah frowned. Something about Ken’s behavior felt strange. He glanced around before quietly moving toward the large bushes lining both sides of the path.","He crouched behind them and waited.","Ken continued walking. After a short distance, he suddenly stopped. Then he slowly turned around.","His eyes swept across the surroundings. He carefully checked the area, making sure no one was following him.","Noah remained completely still.","’He’s checking whether someone is watching him... good thing I hide, after all no one goes to that place...’","Ken seemed satisfied that he was alone and continued toward the back of the dormitory.","Noah narrowed his eyes. ’Something’s definitely wrong.’","He hadn’t remembered Ken being particularly suspicious before. In fact, Ken had fought alongside them during their practical examination against the demons.","’Does he have some kind of important role in the game?’","The thought immediately crossed Noah’s mind. His curiosity won. He decided to follow him.","Noah quietly made his way around the dormitory and reached the rear compound wall.","He carefully hid behind it and peeked around the corner.","Ken was there. But he wasn’t alone.","Another person was standing with him.","Noah recognized her almost immediately.","\"You finally came back.\"","A familiar female voice reached his ears.","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","’Marina Lumineth.’","It was the elf girl who had been part of Noah’s group during the Oakhaven field trip, when they had gone into the wilderness to hunt monsters.","Marina looked relieved to see Ken.","\"Sigh... So, how did things go?\"","\"Better than expected.\"","Ken reached into his belongings.","\"Take this.\"","Noah remained hidden behind the wall. He couldn’t see what Ken had handed her.","Marina stared at the object in her hands. \"Th-This is really an Everbloom Draught?!\"","Her voice trembled with disbelief. \"You actually found one?! How?\"","\"Don’t ask.\" Ken let out a tired sigh. \"I went through a lot of trouble to get it during the vacation.\"","Despite his exhausted tone, Noah could hear a faint hint of satisfaction in his voice.","Marina stared at the potion as though it were a priceless treasure.","\"With this...\" Her voice suddenly became emotional. \"With this, my sister can be cured.\"","\"Huh?!\"","Ken’s voice suddenly became flustered. \"Wait, Marina! Why are you hugging me?!\"","\"Thank you... Thank you, Ken!\"","Marina’s voice trembled as she hugged him tightly.","\"Because of you, my sister can run around again!\"","It sounded as though she was crying.","Noah remained hidden behind the wall.","’Ah... I get it.’","Everything seemed to make sense now.","’Marina must have a younger sister suffering from some kind of illness that can be treated with a rare potion. Ken went through all that trouble to obtain the Everbloom Draught for her.’","Noah nodded to himself.","’That’s why she’s so emotional.’","However something still didn’t feel right. He continued listening.","\"Thank you...\"","Marina’s voice became quieter.","\"I’ll do whatever you want.\"","\"Sure.\"","Ken’s response was calm.","\"But first, give the potion to your sister. Once she’s actually cured, then you can help me.\"","\"Yes.\"","Marina hesitated before continuing.","\"But... to be honest, it’s not going to be easy to arrange a meeting between you and the Elven Queen.\"","Noah’s expression immediately changed.","’...What?’","\"She’s like an elder sister to me,\" Marina continued.","\"And my family is one of the most loyal houses to the royal family. But even so, I can’t guarantee that Her Majesty will agree to meet you.\"","\"Just try.\"","Ken’s voice became serious.","\"You’re the only hope I have.\"","Marina fell silent for a moment.","\"But why do you want to meet Her Majesty?\"","\"It’s something important.\"","Ken’s voice became guarded.","\"I can’t tell you right now.\"","He paused. \"And as a commoner, I have no way of contacting her directly.\"","Noah remained completely silent behind the wall.","His expression gradually became more serious.","’Okay...’","He had initially thought this was simply a matter of Marina’s sister being sick.","But now. ’This is weird.’","Ken had gone through considerable trouble to obtain an extremely rare potion for Marina.","In exchange, he wanted her help arranging a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And whatever he wanted to discuss with her was apparently important enough that he refused to tell Marina about it.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","’I have no idea what’s going on...’","His curiosity grew stronger.","’And what exactly does Ken Takeane want with the Elven Queen? Does he know about something? or does he have future knowledge? Damn what a coincident I found myself into!!’","---","IMPORTANT RANTT OF AUTHOR!!","[A/N: Hello, guys! This is for all the readers who are still sticking with my novel. I genuinely thank you all from the bottom of my heart. If you’re still reading at this point, that means we probably share a similar taste in stories and novels, haha!","Well, I know my last arc involving Akari might have been pretty bad since I stretched it out for quite a while. I apologize for that. I also know that some of you might not like the idea of her joining the harem.","But honestly, I had already decided this a long time ago. So, if you’re still reading, I guess that means you don’t mind it too much. This novel was always meant to be a harem novel, since, well... I’m a harem novel reader myself, haha! Personally, I don’t really like small harems with only two or three girls I’d rather just write a novel with a single FL. Still I’ve decided to limit the harem to five girls for this novel.","Sigh... Anyway, to those of you who are disappointed or sad about this development, I’m sorry. But at the end of the day, I’m writing the story I personally enjoy. If you like this kind of story, I hope you’ll continue reading and enjoying it. And if it’s not your cup of tea, I won’t force you to keep reading.","As for why I’m saying all this... Well, sometimes we authors also feel down and start questioning whether we should continue writing a book or not. So, I just wanted to share a little bit of what was on my mind. Thank you again to everyone who has stayed with the novel this far. I really appreciate you all! ]"]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Browsing Information [1]","paragraphs":["\"Well, let’s meet again later. I’m exhausted and need to get some rest.\"","Ken’s voice reached Noah from the other side of the wall.","’They’re leaving!’","Noah immediately stopped listening. He didn’t want to risk being discovered.","\"Yes, of course. Let’s go.\"","The two of them began walking.","Noah carefully slipped away from the area.","He moved through the bushes without making a sound and only relaxed once he had reached a considerable distance from the dormitory.","He finally let out a quiet breath.","\"Okay...\"","Noah rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","\"Ken is definitely hiding something.\"","He hadn’t known Ken particularly well before, but what he had witnessed today was enough to make him suspicious.","Ken had secretly met Marina behind the dormitory, handed her an extremely rare potion, and in exchange, asked her to arrange a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And whatever he wanted to discuss with the queen was apparently so important that he wasn’t even willing to tell Marina about it.","Noah thought about it for a moment.","’He gave Marina that Everbloom Draught...’","His eyes narrowed.","’What exactly does that potion do?’","If it was valuable enough for Ken to go through considerable trouble to obtain it during his vacation, there had to be more to it.","’I should find out.’","Noah decided to return to his dormitory.","’I can search for information about it on the internet. There should be something about a potion that rare.’","Back inside his dormitory, Noah lay comfortably on his bed with his phone in hand.","Nancy was curled up beside him, peacefully sleeping.","Noah, however, was far too curious to rest. He opened his browser and began searching. He was lucky that the information about this potion existed there, not hidden like some ancient treasure.","\"Everbloom Draught...\"","He scrolled through one page after another.","The potion was more known to world that he thought. No wonder it’s information existed online.","There were articles about rare potions, alchemical records, medical references, historical documents, and discussions written by adventurers and scholars.","Noah continued reading.","\"Hmm...\"","His expression gradually became more serious.","\"It’s really rare...\"","According to several sources, the Everbloom Draught was an exceptionally difficult potion to produce. Even among high-level healing potions, it was considered a precious item because of the number of severe conditions it could treat.","Noah continued scrolling.","\"It can cure several dangerous diseases...\"","He paused.","\"But which one is considered the most dangerous?\"","His eyes moved down the page. Then he stopped. \"Bloodmoon Rot...\"","The name immediately caught his attention.","Noah clicked on the article and began reading carefully.","Bloodmoon Rot was one of the rarest blood-related disease that gradually corrupted the victim’s bloodstream.","As the disease progressed, crimson-colored veins would begin spreading across the victim’s body. The victim would experience an intense and unnatural thirst, recurring high fever, severe weakness, and eventually the failure of vital organs.","Ordinary medicine and conventional antidotes were completely ineffective against it.","Once the disease reached an advanced stage, death was almost inevitable.","Then Noah noticed the treatment.","Treatment: Everbloom Draught","The potion could completely purify the corrupted blood and eliminate the disease from the victim’s body.","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","\"This is...\"","He continued reading.","Then he reached the section describing the origin of the disease.","Known Cause: Vampires.","According to historical and medical records, certain highborn vampires from House Bloodwyn possessed a rare ability to infect their enemies with Bloodmoon Rot. Rather than killing their victims immediately, they could cause their blood to slowly deteriorate, allowing the disease to consume the victim over time.","Noah stared at the screen.","His expression slowly changed.","’Vampires...’","That single word caught his attention far more than anything else on the page.","’If Marina’s sister has this disease...’","His thoughts began connecting the pieces.","’That would mean she was infected by a highborn vampire.’","Noah frowned.","’But that doesn’t make sense.’","Vampires had been extinct for a century. At least, that was what history claimed.","Noah changed the tab of his browser and search for history about vampires. He does know few things from old Noah’s memory. Still he decided to read it again.","The Kingdom of Vespermark had once existed on an island near the Demon Continent.","It had been a small kingdom compared to the major human and elven nations, but the vampires who lived there were notoriously powerful.","Their natural regenerative abilities were extraordinary, and consuming blood allowed them to recover from injuries at an astonishing rate.","Even among supernatural races, vampires were feared for their physical resilience.","But their relationship with humanity and the elves had always been hostile.","Vampires particularly favored the blood of humans and elves, with the blood of high elves being considered especially valuable.","That hostility eventually led to a devastating war.","Humanity and the Elven Kingdom eventually joined forces against Vespermark.","The vampire kingdom was simply too small to withstand two major powers attacking it simultaneously.","Noah continued reading historical records about the conflict.","The war had ended with the complete destruction of Vespermark. The vampires had been hunted down and exterminated. Be it women, children or old people.","According to the historical records, neither side had shown mercy.","Noah’s fingers slowly tightened around his phone.","’They really wiped out the entire race...’","He imagined what that must have looked like.","An entire kingdom surrounded by two powerful nations. There was no realistic way for a small island kingdom to survive such an attack.","It wasn’t really a war anymore. It had become a complete defeat followed by the destruction of an entire people.","A shiver ran down Noah’s spine.","\"That’s... brutal.\"","’There has to be more to this history.’","Noah leaned back against the headboard.","’If vampires really went extinct nearly a hundred years ago, then how could Bloodmoon Rot still be appearing? Maybe Marina’s sister wasn’t suffering from Bloodmoon Rot at all or maybe some vampires from House Bloodwyn had survived.’","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","’If even one highborn vampire survived the destruction of Vespermark, then this changes everything.’","He immediately shook his head.","\"Don’t jump to conclusions.\"","He reminded himself.","’I don’t even know if Marina’s sister has Bloodmoon Rot.’","For all he knew, her illness could be completely unrelated.","Still, the coincidence was too strange to ignore.","Ken had gone through great trouble to obtain an Everbloom Draught.","Marina had said the potion could allow her sister to run around again.","Noah stared at the ceiling.","\"There’s definitely something going on. Let’s see where this potion could be found.\"","He went back to tab of potion’s information. \"The fuck!!\" He couldn’t help but curse after reading more information.","It was written that to make Everbloom Draught potion it needs blood of a highborn vampire who posses that ability to spread disease. It is essential ingredient.","Because of this in current time if there exist this potions in world, then they were extremely rare, biggest chance to found them were within dungeons made by vampires."]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Browsing Information [2]","paragraphs":["He paused. \"I guess I need to study history more seriously too.\"","His curiosity had only grown. He wanted to know more about Vespermark.","More about the vampires.","Noah eventually sat up.","\"Enough thinking. Huge possibility that Ken might be like me... but with knowledge...\"","He placed his phone aside and got out of bed.","Nancy, who had been sleeping comfortably throughout his entire investigation, opened one golden eye because of the sound.","She watched Noah hurriedly walk toward his desk.","\"Meow...\"","Noah glanced back at her.","\"What?\"","Nancy stared at him for a few seconds.","Then she yawned lazily.","\"...\"","She simply closed her eyes again and went back to sleep.","Noah sighed.","\"Right. Of course. Why would you care?\"","He walked over to his desk. After sitting down, Noah reached into his storage ring and took out a thick notebook along with a pen.","This wasn’t an ordinary notebook. It was something Noah had started using specifically for dangerous information.","Whenever something suspicious happened to him, whenever he encountered an incident he couldn’t explain, or whenever he discovered something that might become important later, he wrote it down.","He had learned the hard way that relying entirely on memory was dangerous.","Especially in this world. Noah opened the notebook to a fresh page. He stared at the blank page for a moment.","Then he began writing. The first thing he recorded was the labyrinth.","He carefully documented everything he could remember from the moment he and Damien entered it.","From routes to monsters to the portal. Also the phenomenon happened after Noah vanished in portal.","How those creatures came out from the last boss’s body.","He wrote down every detail he could remember, even things that seemed insignificant.","He deliberately avoided writing anything in a vague manner. If he remembered something clearly, he wrote it down as fact.","After several pages, he reached the events involving Akari.","He carefully recorded how he had encountered her inside the mysterious realm and how they had eventually fought together to survive. he didn’t wrote anything about her bloodline.","He didn’t write down every single detail exactly as it had happened, but he made sure he had enough information to reconstruct the events later.","Eventually, he reached today’s events.","Noah turned to a new section.","Ken Takeane — Suspicious Activity","He began writing.","Ken Takeane was observed secretly meeting Marina behind the dormitory building.","After he was done he rubbed his forehead.","\"Why does everything around me have to be so complicated?\"","He sighed. Then his gaze drifted toward Nancy.","The black cat was still sleeping peacefully on his bed, completely unconcerned with the mysteries threatening to pile up around them.","Noah couldn’t help but smile. \"At least someone here has a peaceful life that I always wish.\"","Nancy’s ears twitched. But she didn’t open her eyes.","Noah kept staring at her then chuckled quietly. Then his expression became serious again.","He looked down at his notebook. \"I need to find out what Ken is planning.\"","He picked up his pen once more. \"And I need to find out whether Marina’s sister actually has Bloodmoon Rot.\"","If she did then the question wouldn’t simply be how she had contracted the disease.","The bigger question would be much more frightening. Were there still vampires alive in this world? If yes then definitely they have some dangerous role in future of this game, in future of this world.","Noah slowly closed the notebook.","Whatever the answer was, he had a feeling that this matter would eventually lead him somewhere he hadn’t expected.","----","\"Yes, Noah? Why did you call me?\"","\"Can’t I call you without a reason now?\" Noah asked, sounding genuinely hurt. \"Sigh... If you really want a reason, then it’s because I missed you.\"","He lay comfortably on his bed with Nancy resting on his chest. One hand gently stroked the little cat’s head, occasionally messing with her fur just to annoy her, while his other hand held the phone to his ear.","He was talking to one of the people dearest to him.","A soft chuckle came from the other end of the call.","\"Haha, don’t be so dramatic. And yes, you can call me even if you don’t have a reason. Just try not to do it when I’m busy.\"","It was Akari’s calm, familiar voice.","\"Hmm... I miss you.\"","\"Yes. Me too. So, did you go to the academy?\"","\"Yeah. Just today.\"","They continued talking for a while, jumping between random topics and casually sharing what had happened since they last spoke. Neither of them seemed particularly interested in ending the call.","After a while, however, Noah remembered the reason he’d wanted to speak with her.","\"Akari, I wanted to ask you something.\"","\"Sure. What is it?\"","\"Hmm...\" Noah hesitated for a moment before asking, \"Do you think vampires are still alive?\"","There was silence on the other end.","Akari didn’t say anything for a while. \"According to the records of our history...\" she finally began, her voice thoughtful, \"they’re supposed to be dead.\"","She continued \"But honestly, I wouldn’t completely believe those records. Vampires weren’t some unintelligent race of beasts or monsters that could simply disappear or get extinct from the world. They were an intelligent race, just like humans and elves.\"","Akari paused briefly.","\"Making an entire intelligent race completely disappear is almost impossible. So, I believe there are definitely some vampires still out there somewhere.\"","\"Hmm... okay.\"","\"But why the sudden interest in vampires?\"","\"Nothing serious. I was studying history and suddenly became curious about them. The war was really cruel.\"","\"Well, that’s how war is,\" Akari replied calmly. \"It happens between races, and sometimes even between humans themselves.\"","She paused before adding,","\"Don’t forget that my family and the Raigamine Duchy was once a separate kingdom. It was only after we lost a war against the Aurelian Empire that our kingdom became part of the empire.\"","\"Oh, right...\"","Noah fell silent for a moment, thinking about her words.","’So Akari also believes that the vampires might still be alive...’","His curiosity only deepened.","---","[A/N: Damn guys!! I actually forgot to upload Chapters yesterday!! I thought i uploaded but i didn’t!! Damn my goldfish memory!! Sorry!!]"]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: Away from Academy","paragraphs":["=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 724 [+112]","Speed: 737 [+120]","Stamina: 720 [+101]","Endurance: 712 [+104]","Charm: 803 [+103]","Mana: 7313 [+1100]","Core Rank: Condensed (High)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.3]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist], [Ice Blizzard], [Crystal Bloom], [Winter Howl]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Abilities: [Adaptive Learning], [Heart of Absolute Frost]","Active Ability: [Monarch’s Decree], [Puppet of the Frost Dragon]","Bloodline: [Monarch of the Frost]","===================","\"Damn, my powers have increased by quite a lot.\"","Noah looked over his status with satisfaction.","He had made tremendous progress in just six months since arriving in this world.","Well... technically, it had been much longer than six months.","He had spent seven months inside that mysterious realm, after all. But from the perspective of the outside world, only a month had passed.","And now, there was something else he wanted to try.","His newly acquired ability.","[Puppet of the Frost Dragon].","’How exactly does this Frost Dragon puppet work?’","He was eager to find out.","It was another morning, and today marked Noah’s first class of the second semester at Novaris Academy.","He glanced at the calendar.","Today was the 24th day of the sixth month, Year 2048.","After getting ready, Noah put on his academy uniform, a gray coat over a white shirt, accompanied by a red tie.","\"Finally, I have to attend lectures again...\"","He sighed and glanced toward the bed.","\"But damn, I’m already bored.\"","His gaze landed on Nancy, who was peacefully sleeping on the bed.","Noah stared at the cat for a few seconds.","\"You sleep all day. You’re so lucky. How good must your life be?\"","He couldn’t help but envy her carefree existence.","Unfortunately, unlike Nancy, he had responsibilities.","There was no point in complaining.","\"Sigh... let’s go. At least the instructor is Morgana. I can handle it.\"","With that, Noah left his dormitory room.","---","\"Is there something on my face?\"","Noah looked toward his left with a slightly confused expression.","Lyria was sitting beside him.","\"No... I mean, you never sat beside me before during class.\"","\"Well, there was a reason—\"","\"Because the two of us sit at the front, he used to avoid sitting beside us. But for some reason, he isn’t doing that anymore.\"","Arisha, sitting on Lyria’s other side, casually interrupted.","She spoke as though it were the most ordinary thing in the world.","\"She’s not wrong.\"","Noah couldn’t help but agree. There was no reason for him to hide it anymore.","\"It’s good to sit in the front. From now on, this is our fixed seat.\"","From Noah’s other side, Damien spoke.","\"Tch. I was hoping Arisha would sit here, but I guess there’s nothing I can do about it now.\"","\"Haha, you really don’t hide what you want.\"","Damien chuckled before patting Noah on the shoulder.","Noah glanced behind him.","A few seats away sat Ophelia.","The moment she noticed Noah’s gaze, she met his eyes and simply gave him a small nod.","Noah returned his attention to the front.","’Now I need to learn as much as possible about these side characters, especially the heroines.’","His expression became slightly thoughtful.","’Who knows? Maybe they have sad stories like Marina’s. I need to look into it.’","Just then, the classroom door opened.","A woman entered the room.","It was Morgana.","Her sky-blue hair was tied into a perfectly neat bun, while her amethyst eyes swept coldly across the entire classroom.","\"It appears everyone is present.\"","She walked toward the instructor’s desk.","\"Welcome back, everyone. The last month has been rather hectic. Monsters suddenly began emerging from an unknown location across various parts of the empire, including Novaris City itself.\"","Morgana placed one hand on the desk.","\"Fortunately, the situation has now been resolved. The academy also had to delay its reopening because of the incident.\"","Her cold gaze swept across the students once more.","\"But now, it is time to refocus on your studies and training.\"","She paused briefly.","\"I hope all of you are ready.\"","\"YES!!!\"","The students answered in unison.","\"Good.\"","Morgana nodded.","\"Now, let’s begin our first lecture.\"","---","Somewhere Far Away from Novaris Academy","In the largest city of the Aurellian Empire, a metropolis far grander than even Novaris City, stood the very heart of the empire.","Aurex Prime.","The magnificent city stretched across the horizon, filled with towering skyscrapers and beautiful modern buildings.","At the heart of the city, overlooking everything from atop a massive hill, stood the imperial palace.","It was enormous.","Its architecture combined modern grandeur with the majesty of an ancient royal fortress.","Inside the vast throne room, massive pillars stood along both sides, supporting the towering ceiling.","At the far end of the chamber was a grand staircase leading toward a majestic black-and-gold throne.","And upon that throne sat a man whose very presence carried the aura of a conqueror.","His dirty-blond hair was neatly combed, while a well-groomed beard framed his masculine features.","One arm rested casually on the throne’s armrest, while his other elbow supported his cheek.","His silver eyes stared forward with an indifferent expression.","He was one of the strongest human across the continent, Viserys Augustus, the Emperor of the strongest Empire, The Aurellian Empire.","A man with white hair stood beside his throne, reporting something to him. He was Baeon, an higher ranking minister in council and trusted person to Emepror.","\"Hmm... so the daughter of Narukami has returned.\"","Viserys’s expression remained indifferent.","\"That’s unexpected. But it is certainly interesting information to receive after I returned to my palace.\"","\"Your Majesty,\" Baeon continued respectfully, \"the monster hordes that had been emerging from the unknown location also stopped appearing and mysteriously perished on the very same day Lady Akari Narukami returned.\"","Viserys’s silver eyes narrowed slightly.","\"And here I have been traveling from place to place, searching for a solution to the situation.\"","His voice remained calm. \"Many others tried as well... yet no one succeeded.\"","He paused for a moment. \"Did you arrange a meeting with her?\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty. I have already sent a message to the Narukami family.\" He bowed his head.","\"Lady Akari has agreed to come here tomorrow to meet with His Imperial Majesty.\"","Viserys leaned back slightly against his throne. A faint glimmer appeared in his indifferent silver eyes."]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: New Dispute","paragraphs":["A week had passed since the academy reopened.","It was now the second week of the semester.","And today, something happened at the academy once again.","The cafeteria was unusually noisy. Students had gathered around something in the middle of the hall, creating a large crowd while excited voices echoed throughout the room.","Noah had just entered the cafeteria with Lyria and Arisha when the commotion immediately caught their attention.","The atmosphere felt strangely familiar.","Noah experienced a sudden sense of déjà vu.","It was almost identical to the atmosphere back when Damien had gotten into a fight with Edward.","\"What’s going on?\" Lyria wondered, looking toward the crowd.","\"Someone must be fighting,\" Arisha replied casually, as though there could hardly be any other explanation.","\"It must be Damien. He probably got into another fight.\"","\"Why do you think it must be him?\" Lyria asked.","\"Who else could it be? Don’t you remember? He got into a fight before, too.\"","\"Yes, but that doesn’t mean—\"","Before Lyria could finish her sentence, a voice from nearby interrupted them.","\"It’s Damien Ashworth! He got into an argument with someone!\"","A student nearby whispered excitedly to his friend before both of them hurried toward the crowd.","The three of them remained where they were for a moment.","\"Sigh... It’s really him,\" Lyria said helplessly. \"We should have joined the crowd earlier.\"","\"It’s Noah’s fault for not being able to finish that potion in time during alchemy class. And as if that wasn’t enough, he stopped both of us from going there with him.\"","Noah completely ignored Arisha’s complaint.","\"Putting that aside, let’s go and see who he’s arguing with this time.\"","The trio made their way through the crowd.","And when they finally reached the center, Noah’s expression changed.","Damien was standing there.","Emma stood behind him.","But opposite them was the last person Noah had expected to see.","A young man with dirty-blond hair and striking silver eyes stood proudly before them. He was handsome, sharp-featured, and roughly the same height as Noah.","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly.","’Prince Justinian Augustus.’","The second prince of the Aurellian Empire.","He was a second-year student at Novaris Academy.","’How the hell did Damien manage to get on his bad side?’","Justinian stood with an elegant, proud posture, his cold eyes fixed on Damien.","\"Damien, you should learn how to speak properly first. Surely, you understand who I am?\"","Damien looked slightly tense.","\"Your Highness, I didn’t mean it that way. I didn’t think you would take offense at what I said.\"","Emma immediately stepped forward and bowed.","\"Please forgive Damien Ashworth, Your Highness.\"","She kept her head lowered.","\"I apologize on his behalf.\"","Damien clenched his fists.","He clearly didn’t like seeing Emma apologize for something that was not her fault.","\"Emma, don’t apologize. You didn’t do anything wrong. And we are not at fault.\"","\"Then you should take responsibility for it, Damien.\"","Justinian took a step forward.","Several people standing behind him, his fellow second-year students and followers, remained silently behind him.","His gaze shifted toward Emma. \"And you are from the Hayes family... A count-ranked family, correct?\"","\"Yes, Your Grace.\"","Emma remained bowed, her voice slightly trembling as fear crept into her heart.","Damien was about to say something when another voice suddenly entered the conversation.","\"Oh my~ If it isn’t our esteemed Prince Justinian Augustus.\"","Everyone in the cafeteria turned toward the newcomer. And it was none other than Noah.","With a polite smile on his face, Noah walked toward Justinian. \"Greetings, Brother Justinian. It has been quite some time since last we crossed paths. I trust you hasn’t forgotten this humble man?\"","Justinian studied Noah for a moment. Then, a faint smirk appeared on his face.","\"Of course I remember you. How could I possibly forget the exiled son of House Eldritch, whose notorious habits were once the talk of noble circles?\"","Damien and Emma looked at Noah in surprise.","Noah, however, showed no reaction to the remark. His smile remained perfectly intact.","He walked forward and positioned himself between Damien and Justinian. \"It is indeed an honor that Your Highness still remembers me.\"","Noah glanced toward Damien before returning his attention to Justinian. \"Yet, judging by the present circumstances, it would seem that my friend has committed some offense against your highness. Though I know not the nature of his transgression, I humbly ask that Your Highness overlook his mistake.\"","Justinian let out a quiet chuckle. \"Oh, Noah. When did I ever say that I intended to punish him?\"","He tilted his head slightly. \"Why do you assume such a thing? Am I truly so fearsome in your eyes?\"","Noah maintained his polite smile. But internally, he was cursing. ’Of course you bastard. I know exactly what kind of piece of shit you are.’","As the son of a duke, Noah had naturally known the second prince since childhood. Justinian possessed everything expected of an imperial prince.","He was handsome, charming, elegant, and dignified. But Noah knew that those qualities were merely a mask.","Behind that refined appearance was a petty, arrogant, and selfish man who looked down upon commoners and rarely tolerated anything that displeased him.","Noah still didn’t know what Damien had said that had offended him.","Justinian’s expression showed no obvious anger. He was even smiling.","Yet Noah knew better. Something was wrong.","’Dammit. We never even crossed paths during the first semester. So why now?’","During the first semester, most of the conflicts had involved first-year students. But now that the second semester had begun,","Noah realized that students from the upper years might become involved as well. And if Justinian was now taking an interest in Damien.","’This is going to bring even more trouble into his life.’","\"Of course not, Your Highness.\" Noah’s smile never faltered.","\"Everyone knows that you to be a most benevolent and generous prince.\"","Justinian’s eyes narrowed slightly at the flattery, though his smile remained.","Noah then turned toward Damien. \"Damien, you should bow and offer them apology. Do not allow others to become entangled in your mistake, nor let another speak on your behalf. If you has earn, then face it by yourself.\"","Damien clenched his fist again. He clearly wasn’t pleased by Noah’s words.","But he glanced around. The crowd had grown considerably larger, and even Emma had bowed before the prince to apologize on his behalf.","Noah’s words were reasonable. After a brief hesitation, Damien finally relented.","He stepped forward and bowed to Justinian. \"I apologize for my mistake. I shouldn’t have said those words.\"","Justinian stared at Damien for a moment.","Then his expression softened into a faint smile.","\"See? It was not so difficult, was it?\" He spoke with the calm confidence of a senior instructing a junior.","\"As thy senior, I merely wished to teach the importance of accepting responsibility for one’s mistakes.\"","His gaze lingered on Damien. \"And you has done well. After all, you are the first-ranked student among the first years, Damien Ashworth.\"","He then looked around the cafeteria. \"And why have all of are gathered here?\"","His tone became slightly amused. \"This is a cafeteria, is it not? You all to be enjoying the meal rather than standing about and watching a trivial dispute.\"","The students immediately began dispersing.","One by one, the crowd returned to their tables, and within moments, the commotion that had filled the cafeteria began to fade.","Just as the situation seemed to be over, however, Justinian’s gaze wandered across the room.","His silver eyes suddenly stopped. They landed on Lyria. For a brief moment, his eyes widened ever so slightly.","Then, slowly his smile grew a little wider."]}]);
